  "instructions": "SQL & JDBC Foundations final check (assessment sql-module-check): the graded final for the whole course. It comes after the Course Review and covers every module, from table design and queries to JDBC data access; the platform sets when you sit it. It is 30 multiple-choice questions with 60 minutes allotted, about 2 minutes per question; there is no timer on each question. The questions are harder than the topic practice quizzes: they ask you to trace, debug and apply ideas from several topics in new situations. Writing SQL and querying a database from Java with JDBC is assessed separately, in the course's graded practical. The assessment platform shows which resources you may use. The pass mark is 70%."
